<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern African Development Community</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as SADC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern African Development Community (SADC) is a regional organisation of 16 states in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, founded in 1992 as successor to the Southern African Development Coordination Conference of 1980. With its secretariat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaborone">Gaborone</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, it promotes economic integration, trade and security cooperation. In 1998 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and Botswana sent troops into Lesotho under its banner after a disputed election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southern-african-development-community.jpg" alt="Southern African Development Community" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_SADC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
